# bumpInstanceName  bumpCellType  x      y      portName  netName
# x and y are the bump's centre in microns, not the PAD centre.
# fake_bumps.lef defines a 29 x 29 um BUMP with a metal5 PAD.
# With this BUMP, the PAD centre is (x - 14.5, y - 14.5).

# Power PADs overlap the existing metal5 parts of the PDN via stacks.
bump_vdd BUMP 84.57 35.50 VDD VDD
bump_vss BUMP 44.57 34.10 VSS VSS

# Signal sites leave room for the footprint and its PAD on the 130 x 130 um die.
# Matching chip-to-chip bumps use the same coordinates on both chiplets.
# The assembly Verilog connects A.clk to B.clk and A.q to B.d.
bump_clk BUMP 25.00 75.00 clk clk
bump_d   BUMP 60.00 75.00 d   d

# B.q is the external output (out_top), not the chip-to-chip data link.
# This bump has no partner on Chip A; external/package wiring is not modeled.
bump_q   BUMP 95.00 105.00 q   q

# These rows place and name signal bumps; signal wires inside the chip
# must still be routed from the standard cells to these PADs.
